<article class="env-lemma" id="066R">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/066R">Lemma <span data-tag="066R">15.76.4</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $(K^\bullet , L^\bullet , M^\bullet , f, g, h)$ be a distinguished triangle in $D(R)$. If two out of three of $K^\bullet , L^\bullet , M^\bullet $ are perfect then the third is also perfect. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Lemmas <a href="/tag/0658" data-tag="0658">15.76.2</a>, <a href="/tag/064V" data-tag="064V">15.66.6</a>, and <a href="/tag/0655" data-tag="0655">15.68.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>